  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe first EDM sub-issue of #290 (design D1):\n- **Machine kinds.** `Kind::WireEdm` / `Kind::SinkerEdm`, declared only (`wire_edm`, `sinker_edm`, plus synonyms such as `wedm` and `die-sinker`). No axis inventory infers an EDM. The required axes are X+Y for wire and Z for sinker. A blank EDM machine has no spindle or coolant.\n- **`.mch` `edm` section** (`crates/post/src/machine/edm.rs`). Wire: lower and upper guide planes, max taper, wire diameters, AWT. Sinker: orbit patterns (CamCraft's geometry name plus the control's word), max orbit radius, pickup. Every key is optional and absent means not stated. Lengths scale with the file's unit. A garbled value refuses the file by name, and the same law is restated in `is_sane` for project files.\n- **No current op family admits an EDM**, so every op is refused at the door on an EDM setup.\n- **Post-time family gate (safety).** `op_streams` now re-checks every op's family against its own setup's machine and refuses by name. Before this, an op made on a mill still posted in a milling dialect after its setup was remounted onto a lathe or an EDM; the door only guarded creation.\n- **No EDM post serves yet** (`post_serves` is false for both kinds).\n- **Templates are test fixtures for now.** The empty wire/sinker templates live in `crates/app/tests/edm/` because every library machine must have a post. They join the library with #533 / #542.\n- `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` documents the kinds and the section.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `edm_machine`, 7/7: templates parse and declare their kinds; a filled section reads and inch-scales; nine garbled values each refuse by name; the kind words round-trip and unknown kinds still refuse; no milling op enters an EDM setup; **a milling op remounted onto an EDM is refused at post, and undo restores the post**; a project round-trips the section.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick`, escalated to batch, 913 s:\n  - geometry, cl, tools, post, sim and motion are green, and clippy `-D warnings` is clean on all 8 crates.\n  - app: green apart from `machine_library`, fixed by the follow-up commit that moved the templates to fixtures. The lathe, turning, mill-turn, drilling, c-axis, program-entry and conformance suites all ran, and the new gate's message appears in none of their logs, so it refused nothing outside its own test.\n  - ui: only the five known reds that are also red on main.\n- After the follow-up: `machine_library` 11/11, `machine` 32/32, `edm_machine` 7/7.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Any real EDM control. No EDM op or post exists yet; this is the schema seam only.\n- The UI machine editor's kind picker still lists only mill, lathe and mill-turn (EDM setup pages are #535).\n\nChangelog: Machine files can declare wire_edm and sinker_edm machines with an edm section; a program whose operation its setup's machine cannot run (an EDM, or a milling op on a setup remounted on a lathe) is refused at post (#530)\n\nFixes #530\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
